WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:06.180
Around 61% of all kerbside rubbish is compostable, so by using the organics bin

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.980
you can make a huge difference to what gets sent to landfill.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:17.720
Let’s start with items that can’t go into
your green bin and should be put in the rubbish.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:22.289
These include non-compostable garden waste
such as cabbage tree leaves and flax.

00:00:22.289 --> 00:00:25.720
Grass clippings from lawns that have been
sprayed in the last six weeks.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.680
And compostable packaging including corn-starch
bags such as this.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:33.920
Items that say commercially compostable
can’t be processed locally

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:35.760
and should go in the rubbish.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.000
So what should go into your bin?

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.500
Food scraps including meat or fish bones

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.200
compostable garden waste

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:48.380
and food-soiled  napkins or cardboard containers, such as pizza boxes.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:53.420
All these items should be loose, not in bags
but you can wrap vege scraps in newspaper.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:02.160
To learn more or to sign up for collection
reminders visit waimakariri.govt.nz/rethinkrubbish

